      "question_text": "A 51- year- old man undergoes a total hip replacement. The surgery was uneventful, and the patient will be discharged to a rehabilitation facility for physical therapy. Nursing staff report that the patient is more anxious and fearful than he was prior to the surgery. The patient acknowledges having trouble sleeping and states he is fearful about leaving the hospital. The mental status exam is otherwise unremarkable. This individual’s presentation is MOST consistent with which of the following diagnoses?",
